cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this instrument, its firmware or its software, please cite the article and this repository."
title: "LIBS elemental imager: design files, firmware and software"
abstract: >-
  Design files, firmware and software of a laboratory laser-induced breakdown
  spectroscopy (LIBS) elemental imager built from low-cost CNC-derived components.
  The stepper step pulses of the scan axis are counted and divided by an
  Arduino-based pulse controller that triggers the laser, which in turn triggers six
  fiber-coupled spectrometers, so that shot spacing is locked to stage position
  instead of to software timing. A Python/PyQt5 application writes compressed
  NetCDF4 hyperspectral cubes; a second application turns them into elemental maps.
